WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
You’ve probably heard this song&nbsp;
sampled in hundreds of Hip Hop tracks.

00:00:09.541 --> 00:00:13.140
But did you know that Bam Bam by&nbsp;
Sister Nancy is a sample itself?

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:19.500
Jamaican dancehall is a genre&nbsp;
that originated during the 1970s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.600
and is rooted in the art of sampling.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.960
So when Sister Nancy was in the studio in 1982,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.760
she was inspired by Yellowman who had&nbsp;
created a Bam Bam song around the same time.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:39.420
But Yellowman’s chorus actually originates&nbsp;
in the 1966 song Bam Bam by The Maytals.

00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:44.340
Sister Nancy then completely freestyled new lyrics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.700
on top of a different beat pulled&nbsp;
from Stalag 17 by Ansel Collins.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.680
So now when you hear a rap&nbsp;
song sample Bam Bam today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.860
you’ll know that song is a&nbsp;
sample of a sample of a sample.

